AngelSlim — VecAttention NOTICE
===============================

VecAttention is the sparse-attention algorithm whose
in-tree code is ORIGINAL AngelSlim work (Apache-2.0, see the file headers under
`algorithms/vecattention/`). Its method (per query-block MinP column selection:
`gap = -log(threshold)`; keep key `j` iff `qk[j] + gap >= max_j qk`, plus an
attention-sink block and a local band) is implemented here as original code.

This NOTICE records the provenance of the two non-original pieces this algorithm
touches, so a released wheel carries a complete license/attribution trail.

1. Real kernel — `vllm_flash_attn.sparse_attn_func` (EXTERNAL, not vendored here)
   ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
   The fast path calls `sparse_attn_func` from a vLLM-flash-attention fork. That
   fork is NOT vendored into this tree and is NOT a git submodule of this repo —
   it is an EXTERNAL optional dependency, consumed as an environment-installed
   package (`pip install vllm_flash_attn`, or a local editable build of the
   fork). The fork is a 440 MB compiled CUDA project; tracking it in-repo (as a
   submodule or vendored source) was removed in favor of treating it like any
   other external compiled kernel (the way the other algorithms depend on an
   installed `triton`). The fork bundles its own third-party code, EACH under its
   own license, which travels with the fork (not with AngelSlim):
     - vLLM flash-attention (Apache-2.0)
     - Dao-AILab FlashAttention (BSD-3-Clause)
     - NVIDIA CUTLASS (BSD-3-Clause)
   AngelSlim ships NONE of these in-tree; they are recorded here only because the
   vecattention fast path links against them at runtime. On head_dim 256 (Qwen3.5)
   and on any box where the kernel is not installed, vecattention falls back to
   the pure-torch reference (`reference.py`, original Apache-2.0 code) — so the
   algorithm is usable with NO third-party kernel present.

   Distribution note: the fork is not yet publicly cloneable over HTTPS; until it
   is republished under a public org (or published to PyPI), treat vecattention as
   REFERENCE-ONLY for external users (the kernel fast path is unavailable to
   them). If a contributor keeps a
   local build of the fork under `vecattention/ops/vllm-flash-attention/`, that
   path is .gitignored and never tracked.

2. Autotune config caches — `ops/cache/*.pkl`
   ------------------------------------------
   `dit_vecattention_kernels_best_eff_configs.pkl` /
   `vlm_vecattention_kernels_best_eff_configs.pkl` are AngelSlim-generated Triton
   autotune config dictionaries (block sizes / num_warps per shape) — original
   Tencent artifacts, no third-party content. They are plain config mappings.

